	Here at school, we have a policy that users must sign a set of
	'user guidelines' before they get their account.  These guidelines
	basically lay out what the users rights and responsibilities are,
	and what the staffs rights and responsibilities are.

	One of the staff rights is the ability to view any file on the
	system (including /var/spool/mail/*) IF NEEDED.  Thus, if some
	emergency were to come up, the staff would be allowed to view these
	files.  However, this would only come after much consultation with
	the systems manager, and many attempts to come to a different 
	solution.

	In general, we want to protect the privacy of users, and will not go
	grab a users file (even if it is globally readable) without their
	permission---but it was felt that this right was something that 
	might prove handy, in lieu of some annoyingly bored students we had
	a few summers ago.

	Most students and profs have agreed that the scheme is reasonable,
	and only a few have expressed reservations...

	It's a touchy situation, with no completely satisfying answer.


