Who is harrassing whom?

You seem to be complaining that Larry Colton is harrassing you, yet your
message reads as an attempt to harrass Larry Colton.

You justify your actions as "research" but the nature of that research
is completely unspecified.  You say nothing of what it was that Larry
Colton objected to.

If Larry Colton, or anybody, suspects you are doing something improper,
it is appropriate for him to bring it to the attention your system
administrator by sending email to postmaster and/or root.  If his
complaints are unjustified, your system administrator should simply
ignore them.  If the complaints are unjustified, and if your system
administrator is nevertheless punishing you for unjustified complaints,
then it is your system administrator who is harrassing you.  If Larry
Colton is repeatedly sending messages to your sysadmin, then he is
harrassing your sysadmin, not you.

Your post basically amounts to "he did bad; I did good; I'm not going
to tell you what it was all about; please help me anyway."  If you cannot
do better than that, you should not expect much help.

